### Run these from IntelliJ (or VS Code REST Client). The app must be running with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set.

### 0. Zero-shot, no system prompt: notice how long and generic the answer is
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/zero-shot
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "Review this Java: for (int i = 0; i <= list.size(); i++) { System.out.println(list.get(i)); }"}

### 1. SAME code, with a system prompt (role + rules + format)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/review
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "for (int i = 0; i <= list.size(); i++) { System.out.println(list.get(i)); }"}

### 2. Few-shot: three examples teach the format
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/commit-message
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "I made the login page show an error when the password is wrong"}

### 3. Chain of thought: plan first, then code; the API returns the code part separately
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/generate-method
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "A method that returns true if a String is a palindrome, ignoring case, spaces and punctuation."}

### 4. Structured output: JSON we can validate and use
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/extract-task
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "I need to submit the AI design document by next Friday, it's urgent"}

### 4b. Try to break it: no date given → dueDate must be null (not invented)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/extract-task
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "water the plants"}

### 5. Pair programming lab: weak prompt v1, improve it in Prompts.java and re-run
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/interview-questions
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "junior Java"}

### Validation: blank input → 400, no call to Claude
POST http://localhost:8080/api/prompts/review
Content-Type: application/json

{"input": "   "}
